Suppose that $\Gamma^{(0)}(T(m),v)$ is cellular. Then so is $e\Gamma^{(0)}(T(m),v)e$ by Lemma \ref{C Lem idem}. 
However, we find that there is no matrix $\bD$ with entries in $\ZZ_{\ge0}$ that satisfies the condition $\bD^T\bD=\bC$, a contradiction.

Next, we show that the algebra $\Gamma^{(0)}(T(1),v)$ is cellular. It is easy to see that the anti-involution $\iota$  
